      "text": "Chūzan became a tributary of Ming China in 1372; Nanzan followed in 1380 and Hokuzan in 1383. In 1392 Ming sent thirty-six Chinese families from Fujian to manage the kingdom's trade. The kingdom sold Japanese silver, swords, fans and lacquerware and Chinese herbs, coin, ceramics and silk, and bought sappanwood, rhinoceros horn, tin, sugar, iron, ambergris, Indian ivory and Arabian frankincense."
